--- !u!114 &-2864662184569546130
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 456c7c2b477e4253b9e4faf9ed4b18a9, type: 3}
  m_Name: InstructionsParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.InstructionsParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Title:
    m_Untranslated: Instructions
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "<b>1.</b>  Reopen the <b>Collectible</b> script in your script
      editor.\n\n<b>2.</b>  Modify the rotation line in the <b>Update()</b> method
      to <b>transform.Rotate(0, 0.5f, 0);.</b>\n \nThis change reduces the rotation
      speed to half a degree per frame. \n\nWhen entering the decimal value <b>0.5,</b>
      make sure to add \u201Cf\u201D at the end (0.5f). Try temporarily removing
      the \u201Cf\u201D to see the error in your code.\n\n<b>3.</b>  Save the script
      and return to the Unity Editor. Play your scene to observe the slower rotation
      of the collectible."
  m_CriteriaCompletion: 0
  m_Criteria:
    m_Items: []
--- !u!114 &-2574609763360475036
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "Congratulations on writing your first line of code to make the
      collectible rotate about the Y-axis! \n\nHere are some of the things you learned
      along the way:\n\n\u2022 Explain the <b>using</b> statements at the top of
      a Unity script. (<a href='https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/Namespaces.html?utm_source=learnTPOCi'>more</a>)\n\u2022
      Identify a class declaration in a script. (<a href='https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/Namespaces.html?utm_source=learnTPOCi'>more</a>)\n\u2022
      Explain the MonoBehaviour class in Unity scripts. (<a href='https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/class-MonoBehaviour.html?utm_source=learnTPOCi'>more</a>)\n\u2022
      Explain the <b>Start</b> method and <b>Update</b> method in a Unity script.
      (<a href='https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/CreatingAndUsingScripts.html?utm_source=learnTPOCi'>more</a>)\n\u2022
      Call a transform function in the <b>Update</b> method to transform a GameObject
      over time. (<a href='https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/EventFunctions.html?utm_source=learnTPOCi'>more</a>)\n\u2022
      Apply correct data types in code, including integers and floats.\n\u2022 Declare
      new custom variables in a script. (<a href='https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/VariablesAndTheInspector.html?utm_source=learnTPOCi'>more</a>)\n\u2022
      Explain how public variables in a script behave in Unity. (<a href='https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/VariablesAndTheInspector.html?utm_source=learnTPOCi'>more</a>)\n\u2022
      Describe common naming conventions including PascalCase and camelCase.\n\u2022
      Apply correct naming conventions to variables and methods.\n"
